1
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,320
Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,577
Yu-Gi-Oh!

3
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,897
Yu-Gi-Oh! ending

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:15,980
the

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:17,450
game!

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,980
Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu-Gi-Oh!

7
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:05,102
I wonder if these virtual
berries have any taste.

8
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,560
I feel like I haven't eaten in months.

9
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,257
Hey, do you think anyone's
serving food in that shack?

10
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,280
I doubt it.

11
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,500
Hmm, a house in the middle of the woods.

12
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,899
This seems a little too convenient.

13
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,857
You think it's another one
of Noah's virtual traps?

14
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:27,160
Just let me open it and stay
right next to me, Mokuva.

15
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,800
What? Hold on.

16
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:33,300
It's our stepfather's old house.

17
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,340
Another blast from our past.

18
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:44,180
Look, it's a virtual projection of our
first day in this house. That's right.

19
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:47,920
It's the day Gozaburo took
us home from the orphanage.

20
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,500
And it was no picnic.

21
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,170
Now,

22
00:01:51,253 --> 00:01:54,497
if a train from Boston is
traveling at 180 miles per

23
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:57,377
hour and a train from New York
is traveling at the same...

24
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,290
Wake up!

25
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:02,520
I sincerely apologize for
interrupting your lesson, Professor.

26
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:07,114
But it seems young Seto was more
concerned with the backs of his eyelids.

27
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,110
Continue.

28
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,540
I have strict orders.

29
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,580
My boss has no patience
for slackers. What?

30
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:14,860
I don't slack!

31
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:17,827
I hear you're falling
behind in your studies.

32
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:23,885
So you'll no longer have the
weekends off, starting immediately.

33
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,800
But I've been working so hard.

34
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,560
Not hard enough.

35
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:32,180
You must have discipline, Seto.

36
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:34,693
It's the only way to crush your enemies.

37
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,360
But I don't have enemies.

38
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:38,960
Of course you do.

39
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,017
You're just not aware of them yet.

40
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:45,700
You have to learn that you can
trust no one at all, including me.

41
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:47,970
Thompson!

42
00:02:48,053 --> 00:02:49,759
Confiscate Seto's toys immediately!

43
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:51,620
Yes, sir.

44
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:56,557
Maybe now you'll concentrate on your
studies instead of wasting your brain away.

45
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,400
Well, that ought to do it.

46
00:02:58,540 --> 00:03:00,000
It's for your own good.

47
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:05,160
Your stepfather's a very wise man, and
I think he knows what's best for you.

48
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:07,633
So I'd advise you not to disappoint him.

49
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:14,940
The way they treat Seto stinks,
but I know how to make him smile.

50
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,820
Well, here goes.

51
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,430
Excuse me.

52
00:03:21,513 --> 00:03:22,940
Hey, back to bed.

53
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:26,680
Okay, but first I gotta
give Seto his textbook back.

54
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,360
You heard Dad.

55
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,369
Gotta study, study, study.

56
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:34,980
If I see one more textbook,
I think I'm gonna barf.

57
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,520
Sleeping? Already?

58
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,428
You still have one more
lesson left tonight.

59
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,857
And you left this textbook behind.

60
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:46,760
If I were you, I'd be
more careful next time.

61
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,620
Whatever you say, Hobson.

62
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,800
Your next lesson's in one hour.

63
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,680
I can't take this!

64
00:03:58,460 --> 00:04:01,480
Dear Seto, I guess you
found my hiding place.

65
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:05,331
Remember, big bro, they can't
take away everything from us.

66
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:09,980
So enjoy my gift, but don't let them
find it. Love, Moki. Thanks, bro.

67
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,420
My Duel Monsters cards.

68
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,420
Well, they're not the greatest
cards, but they're mine. Huh?

69
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,540
A Blue-Eyes White Dragon?

70
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:22,120
Mokuba made me a Blue-Eyes card.

71
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:27,240
One day, I know I'll have the
real thing in my deck. Just wait.

72
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,070
Huh?

73
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,820
A good show by the Kaiba Boys.

74
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:40,157
That trip down memory lane really
pulls at the heartstrings, doesn't it?

75
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:43,640
Noah, we've had enough of
your sick and twisted games.

76
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,697
Why, the game's only just begun.

77
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:50,840
So get ready to relive every painful
moment of your entire lives. What?

78
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,940
It's gonna be a very bumpy ride.

79
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,360
Look, kid, what do you
expect to gain from this?

80
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,833
Everything that should have
been mine from the beginning.

81
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:07,232
This game's pretty easy.

82
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:12,077
The stars above each door represent the
strength of the monster behind that door.

83
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,657
Beat the monster and get through.

84
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,417
There's a clue we're missing.

85
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,740
But what can it be?

86
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,130
I know.

87
00:05:18,213 --> 00:05:22,117
Maybe the stars represent more than
just the power level of the monsters.

88
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,500
But what, Yugi?

89
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,800
Well, what if they're
like directions for us?

90
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:32,062
Yeah, through the one star door first, then
the two, then the three, then the four.

91
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,050
Yes,

92
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:36,137
and the reason you and I have been
traveling around in circles is because

93
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:40,177
we've only been choosing to battle
against the monsters that have one star.

94
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,920
Well, let's try this door.

95
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,980
So now I play...

96
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,420
Obnoxious Celtic Guardian!

97
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,190
Attack!

98
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:54,060
Well done.

99
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,960
Now, let's go through and find Taya!

100
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,037
A bit brisk, isn't it?

101
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,860
I can't even feel my toes.

102
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:07,780
Advantage number 204 of being a penguin.

103
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,515
We have thermo-insulated flipper feet.

104
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:13,260
Now, let's get back to business, shall we?

105
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,580
Be strong.

106
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:18,100
All right, let's do this. Good.

107
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:23,144
The sooner you make your move, the sooner
I can freeze you over and win this duel.

108
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:27,497
You're already knee-deep in ice, and
the worst is yet to come, my dear.

109
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:32,462
My all-powerful Flying Penguin is ready to
soar straight through your puny defense!

110
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,510
No!

111
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:35,757
If his Flying Penguin
attacks, I'll be wide open!

112
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:39,937
And if I place you on the playing field
to defend me, then he'll just destroy you!

113
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,100
So very true.

114
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:43,980
And if your Deckmaster is destroyed,

115
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:47,460
well, then you automatically
lose the duel, my dear.

116
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:53,617
I'll place one monster face down in defense
mode, and then I'll end my turn, Krump.

117
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:58,120
An extremely desperate move for
an extremely desperate girl.

118
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:01,100
And my hand continues
to grow more powerful.

119
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,820
And now, take this!

120
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:06,360
Flying penguin attack!

121
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:12,690
Ha!

122
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,820
There goes your face down card.

123
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,780
Now you're back where
you started. Not quite.

124
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:21,431
You revealed my scalangle,
which lets me draw one new card.

125
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,060
Magic formula.

126
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:26,617
this may come in handy
i ran the numbers and

127
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,037
you've run out of luck
so play whatever pathetic

128
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,497
card you'd like because
it's only a matter of

129
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:34,357
time before you're
frozen here forever or my

130
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:37,997
name isn't adrian
randolph from the third a

131
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:41,377
master in the art of
number crunching i must say

132
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:46,497
and best dressed penguin
in the world you are a

133
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,700
weird little bird crump
and i'm in the mood for

134
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:52,350
a barbecue.

135
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:53,880
What's this? Mahavailo?

136
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:56,380
No, he's not powerful enough.

137
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:57,776
There's no way he'll

138
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,497
beat Flying Penguin.

139
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,740
Taya, don't give up so fast.

140
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:04,260
He has a secret skill that can help

141
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,430
you. Huh?

142
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:08,020
What kind of a skill?

143
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,420
Hold on.

144
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:10,577
I remember this.

145
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,307
Yugi once told me about this

146
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,030
card.

147
00:08:15,113 --> 00:08:17,208
You want to know which
card is most like me?

148
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,440
Wait, I know.

149
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:20,080
Well, I think I know.

150
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,150
It's that

151
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:23,697
purple guy with the big hat, right?

152
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:25,137
Uh, big hat?

153
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,420
Oh, you mean my Dark Magician card.

154
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,510
Well, even

155
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:32,877
though it's pretty great, I don't think
it's the card that's most like me.

156
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:33,790
Okay.

157
00:08:33,873 --> 00:08:35,120
Ah, this is the

158
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:37,120
Pretty cool, right?

159
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,300
Maha Vilo?

160
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,467
He may not be as strong
as the Dark Magician.

161
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:45,037
Well, not when you first
look at him anyway.

162
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:48,800
But if you look closer, you'll
see a hidden power deep inside.

163
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,600
Of course!

164
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,155
It's hidden strength!

165
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,080
I'm not done yet!

166
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:59,360
Now I summon Maha Vilo in attack mode!

167
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,820
That's weak! Wait!

168
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:03,937
I'm not done!

169
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:08,220
Check this out, I activate magic formula!

170
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:11,760
Raising my monster's attack points by 500!

171
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,077
You must have failed all
of your math courses, kid,

172
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:19,217
because it's still too short on attack
points to defeat my flying penguin.

173
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:22,476
I guess you don't know about
Mahavailo's hidden power.

174
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:26,560
He gets 500 extra attack points
for each one of my magic cards.

175
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,680
No fair!

176
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,220
Oh, it's fair!

177
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,797
Go Mahavailo!

178
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:36,420
Attack his flying penguin
with sacred lightning!

179
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,080
Add this up, crump!

180
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:52,900
Extra crispy fried penguin, anyone?

181
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,720
We're safe, at least for now.

182
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,780
I'm freezing!

183
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:06,480
I don't know how much
longer I can last out here.

184
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:08,036
We're getting close.

185
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,947
Yeah, Taya's getting louder.

186
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,480
Time is running out.

187
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,597
Yami and I have to defeat more
of Noah's monsters so we can get

188
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:20,540
through this virtual maze and
find Taya before it's too late.

189
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:22,721
I see another set of doors ahead.

190
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,680
We need the three-star door.

191
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,140
There it is.

192
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:31,970
Yes!

193
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:35,740
Swift Gaia, the Fierce Knight! Attack!

194
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:38,640
No, stop the attack! Huh?

195
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:40,260
It's too late!

196
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,090
Gaia!

197
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:50,107
That door has been
equipped with a trap card.

198
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,892
Look more closely, right under the stars.

199
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,940
Three face down cards! Of course!

200
00:10:57,240 --> 00:11:00,177
Then that blast had to be
a Mirror Force trap card.

201
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:01,640
So, try again.

202
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,290
Here goes!

203
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:05,460
I summon Gazelle!

204
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:12,760
It looks like Dark King of the
Abyss, a weaker monster. Awesome!

205
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:15,940
Say goodbye! No, wait!

206
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,751
Another face-down card is being activated.

207
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:19,939
Now it's stronger!

208
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,260
Then I summon Burpament!

209
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,520
Then I'll use this!

210
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:30,770
Polymerization!

211
00:11:30,853 --> 00:11:34,020
Fuse them together to form Chimera!

212
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:36,620
Now attack, my mythical beast!

213
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,080
Yes! Let's go!

214
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:48,780
Now, where's that four-star monster?

215
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:50,620
There it is!

216
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:51,642
Patience, Yugi.

217
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:53,500
You must be very careful.

218
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:56,420
This door has been
equipped with five cards.

219
00:11:57,400 --> 00:12:00,657
Noah could have hidden just
about anything behind that door.

220
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:03,420
And you're low on cards, so choose wisely.

221
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,070
You're right.

222
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,006
I only have a few cards left.

223
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:11,720
Defeating a four-star monster plus
four face-down cards is no easy task.

224
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:14,380
This may do it.

225
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:17,840
No, you mustn't play
Dark Magician yet. Okay.

226
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:22,140
Then how about the Heavy Storm Magic card?

227
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,077
It destroys all magic and trap cards.

228
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,520
Nice work.

229
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:31,446
Now his monster stands alone.

230
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:34,060
With no face down cards to protect it.

231
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:36,760
Destroy it, Yugi.

232
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:40,560
Four-star Lady Bug of
Duke should do the trick.

233
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,260
It may seem weak, but watch this.

234
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,660
It automatically destroys
all four-star monsters.

235
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,940
Oh, yeah!

236
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,360
Excellent move. Thanks!

237
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:03,697
It's a good thing I had that
little critter stashed in my deck.

238
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:05,237
This could be the last door.

239
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,150
Come on!

240
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,450
Taya!

241
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:12,580
This doesn't look good.

242
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,080
Don't worry, Taya! Stay strong!

243
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:16,860
I'm right here for you!

244
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,160
All right, Dad.

245
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:21,140
I play Bolt Penguin.

246
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:27,000
And as an extra precaution,
I'll play one card face down!

247
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:31,160
Your little turkey only
has 800 defense points!

248
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,929
I can stuff it and
roast it with one blast!

249
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:36,440
So stand back, Crump!

250
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,530
Mahavailo!

251
00:13:38,613 --> 00:13:40,360
Attack his bullpen twin now!

252
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:48,717
All my calculations
were right out of money!

253
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:52,320
Now I activate Revenge Sacrifice!

254
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,460
Goodbye, Mahavailo!

255
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,680
No, not him!

256
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:04,200
Revenge Sacrifice destroys the
card you used to attack my monster!

257
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:07,980
And now I'll defend
myself with this monster!

258
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,960
The impenetrable Defender Iceberg!

259
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:19,682
Check that out!

260
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:22,100
It's like a giant ice cube! Yes!

261
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:26,060
A giant ice cube with
2,450 defense points!

262
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,597
You'll never get past that!

263
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,151
And don't think I'm done!

264
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,200
I'll place this face down...

265
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:33,540
and summon Penguin Torpedo!

266
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:37,400
This little bird is a real blast, kid!

267
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,540
Especially when my Deck Master
ability gets it a boost!

268
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:47,400
I almost forgot it can attack
your life points directly!

269
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:58,520
And since you lost a chunk of life,
point, you've gained another chunk of ice.

270
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,960
Yes, it's quite chilling, isn't it?

271
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,200
Look, Crump, I'm not out yet.

272
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:06,688
These two cards won't help.

273
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:07,817
I'm out of moves.

274
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:10,200
There is one thing you can do, Teya.

275
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,420
Move me onto the playing field.

276
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,760
Trust me, it's your last hope.

277
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:16,884
I guess I have nothing to lose.

278
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:20,340
I move Dark Magician Girl to the field!

279
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:24,037
Don't you realize if your
Deckmaster is destroyed, you lose?

280
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:27,160
You must have a pathetic
hand to make that move!

281
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,240
Now watch and learn!

282
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:35,320
I activate Ocean of Regeneration and
bring back my old friend, Penguin Torpedo!

283
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,757
This magic card allows
me to bring any water

284
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:41,428
monster back from my
graveyard for one turn!

285
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:42,660
Penguin Torpedo!

286
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,158
Attacker life points directly again!

287
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:53,950
Nooo!

288
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:58,680
Suddenly, I'm in the mood for
a tall glass of ice, Teya!

289
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:07,760
Soon I'll return to the
real world as a Freemur!

290
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:10,900
Leave her alone! Teya!

291
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:14,737
If she loses this duel,
she'll be trapped here!

292
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:16,320
but it's not fair.

293
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:20,780
She's not experienced enough
and she's losing badly.

294
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:26,240
Teya can win, Yugi, by trusting herself
and believing in the heart of the cards.

295
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,837
I'm down to my last few life
points and my dark magician

296
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:35,597
girl isn't strong enough
to get past his defense.

297
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:40,092
Plus, since she's my deck master, if
she's destroyed, I automatically lose.

298
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:44,257
Teya, there is one card in
your deck that can save us.

299
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:46,164
It's the first card you picked.

300
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,720
Wait, is it the Sage's Stone Magic card?

301
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:51,860
Yes, Taya.

302
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:54,121
That's the card you need to draw.

303
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:58,020
But it could be at the bottom
of my deck for all I know.

304
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:01,340
I will help you draw
this card. To do this,

305
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,337
I must first invoke my
Deckmaster's special ability

306
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:06,957
to call upon every
monster in your graveyard,

307
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:07,870
Taya.

308
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:09,370
Behold!

309
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,180
Dark Magic Energies!

310
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:12,857
Please hear my call!

311
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:16,469
Come on, enter our graveyard
and revive the monsters within!

312
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,580
What's going on?

313
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:28,200
Taya, I have formed a soul circle with
the four monsters in your card graveyard.

314
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,980
This allows you to draw four new cards.

315
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,320
The rest is up to you.

316
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:38,540
Let's see, did I draw the card I need?

317
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,090
Yes,

318
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:46,600
there it is Now to play
it Stupid ice There,

319
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:50,820
did it So what exactly does this card do?

320
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,580
What's up with my dual disc?

321
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:58,590
Wow

322
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:04,060
My dark magician But how was he summoned?

323
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:09,390
Huh?

324
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,760
Dark Magician?

325
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:18,060
I have no idea where he came
from, but I am not complaining.

326
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:20,610
What?

327
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:24,376
My calculations assured me
that I would win this duel!

328
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:26,500
This just doesn't add up at all!

329
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:31,357
The power of the Sage of Stone Magic
card bestows upon me the unique

330
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:35,277
ability to call forth the Dark
Magician from any nearby player's deck.

331
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,190
What?

332
00:18:36,273 --> 00:18:37,103
It can't be!

333
00:18:37,186 --> 00:18:39,240
Double Dark Magic Attack!

334
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,960
Our task is complete.

335
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:07,360
Whoa, I won!

336
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,670
Teya?

337
00:19:14,753 --> 00:19:15,720
Can you hear me?

338
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:18,690
Teya!

339
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:20,540
You did it!

340
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:22,540
Oh, Yugi!

341
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:25,620
I was almost a human ice pop!

342
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,240
I'm so glad to see you!

343
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,660
Me too, Teya!

344
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:36,431
And now that we're together,
I promise it'll stay that way!

345
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,300
How cute!

346
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:41,880
Little do they realize I'm
just getting warmed up, fools!

347
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:46,540
They'll never escape my
virtual universe! Never!
